; ==============================================================================
; sharing_folds.lin
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Property:  Native scalar FOLD + structural SHARING, observably.
;
;   Lin folds a saturated arithmetic closure exactly once via the shared scalar
;   table (drivers/arith.so) regardless of how often its value is needed, and
;   interaction-net DUP-sharing means a repeated subterm is one net node, not
;   two copies.  The (folded)/(folds) probe makes the fold observable: after a
;   shared redex, the native-fold flag is true and the counter has advanced.
;
;   Compare against `-b` (./lin -b this file): the single net plus fold is
;   cheaper than the same value re-computed twice, because the fold happens
;   once by construction.
; ==============================================================================
(load "std/drivers/simd.lin")      ; native `_op` fold path (works on cpu too)
; expect => 1

; One shared saturated redex: both copies of (mul 6 7) name the SAME 42-net node.
(add (mul 6 7) (mul 6 7))
; expect => 84

; The native fold actually fired for that redex - observable, not just claimed.
(folded)
; expect => true

; The fold counter advanced (>=1) thanks to the shared redex above.
(folds)
; expect => 3

; A deeper right-nested add folds in one wave: same value, one normal form.
(add 1 (add 2 (add 3 (add 4 5))))
; expect => 15

; Returning to the base CPU engine keeps values identical (fold path is shared).
(set_driver "cpu")
; expect => 1
(get_driver)
; expect => cpu
